# ACT I - The Beginning

## Chapter 1: Basic Elements

= This synopsis introduces the basic elements of Fountain syntax

INT. TEST LOCATION - DAY

Basic action line that describes what's happening in the scene.

!FORCED ACTION: This action line is forced with an exclamation mark.

JOHN DOE enters the room carrying a briefcase.

                    JOHN DOE
          This is basic dialogue.

                    JOHN DOE (CONT'D)
          This is continued dialogue from the
          same character.

                    JANE SMITH
                    (whispering)
          This dialogue has a parenthetical.

                    JOHN DOE (O.S.)
          This is off-screen dialogue.

                    NARRATOR (V.O.)
          This is voice-over narration.

@COMPUTER VOICE
Computer-generated or special character.

~MARY sings softly
This is a lyric or special speech format.

[[This is a note that won't appear in the final output]]

/*
This is a boneyard comment.
Multiple lines can be included here.
These won't appear in the final script.
*/

                    JOHN DOE ^
          This is dual dialogue on the left.

                    JANE SMITH ^
          This is dual dialogue on the right.

The dual dialogue continues with both characters speaking simultaneously.

                    JOHN DOE ^
          Left side continues.

                    JANE SMITH ^
          Right side continues.

MONTAGE - VARIOUS LOCATIONS

A) First montage element
B) Second montage element
C) Third montage element

END MONTAGE

                         CUT TO:

EXT. OUTDOOR LOCATION - LATER

More action describing the outdoor scene.

FADE TO BLACK.

                         DISSOLVE TO:

.FORCED SCENE HEADING

This scene heading was forced with a period at the beginning.

                    CHARACTER WITH EMPHASIS
          This dialogue contains *emphasis* and
          **bold text** and _underlined_ text.

                    ANOTHER CHARACTER
          This is a longer speech that goes on
          for multiple lines to test how the
          parser handles extended dialogue
          blocks.

> CUSTOM TRANSITION <

Another action line after the custom transition.

### Chapter 2: Advanced Elements

= Synopsis for the advanced elements section

INT. COMPLEX LOCATION - NIGHT

The action continues with more complex elements.

                    MAIN CHARACTER
          What do you think about this?

                    SUPPORTING CHARACTER
                    (thinking)
          I'm not sure... let me consider
          this carefully.

                    MAIN CHARACTER
                    (interrupting)
          We don't have time to think!

The character RUNS toward the door.

                    MAIN CHARACTER (CONT'D)
                    (shouting)
          Come on! We have to go NOW!

SOUND EFFECT: LOUD EXPLOSION

Everyone ducks for cover.

                    SUPPORTING CHARACTER
                    (panicked)
          What was that?!

                    MAIN CHARACTER
          I don't know, but we need to get
          out of here.

They rush toward the exit.

                    MAIN CHARACTER (CONT'D)
                    (calling back)
          Follow me and stay close!

INTERCUT - PHONE CONVERSATION

                    PERSON A
                    (on phone)
          Hello? Are you there?

                    PERSON B
                    (on phone)
          Yes, I can hear you. What's the
          situation?

                    PERSON A
                    (on phone)
          It's worse than we thought.

END INTERCUT

BACK TO SCENE

The characters continue their escape.

                    MAIN CHARACTER
          We made it! We're safe now.

                    SUPPORTING CHARACTER
                    (relieved)
          Thank goodness. I thought we
          weren't going to make it.

A moment of silence as they catch their breath.

                    MAIN CHARACTER
          This isn't over yet.

                         MATCH CUT TO:

INT. SECRET LOCATION - CONTINUOUS

A mysterious figure watches security monitors.

                    MYSTERIOUS FIGURE
                    (to subordinate)
          They escaped. But it doesn't matter.
          We know where they're going.

                    SUBORDINATE
          Should we pursue them?

                    MYSTERIOUS FIGURE
          Not yet. Let them think they're
          safe. We'll strike when they least
          expect it.

===

# ACT II - The Middle

## Chapter 3: Conflict Escalation

= The conflict begins to escalate in this section

EXT. ABANDONED WAREHOUSE - DAWN

The sun rises over an industrial landscape.

Our heroes approach cautiously.

                    MAIN CHARACTER
                    (whispered)
          Remember the plan. We go in quiet,
          get what we came for, and get out.

                    SUPPORTING CHARACTER
                    (nodding)
          Got it. What if we run into
          trouble?

                    MAIN CHARACTER
          Then we improvise.

They move toward the entrance.

CLOSE-UP - DOOR HANDLE

A hand reaches for the handle and slowly turns it.

BACK TO SCENE

The door creaks open.

                    MAIN CHARACTER
                    (looking inside)
          It's too quiet. Something's not
          right.

                    SUPPORTING CHARACTER
          Maybe they're not here.

                    MAIN CHARACTER
          Or maybe it's a trap.

They exchange worried glances.

                    MAIN CHARACTER (CONT'D)
          Only one way to find out.

They step inside.

                         SMASH CUT TO:

INT. WAREHOUSE - CONTINUOUS

The space is dark and filled with shadows.

                    MYSTERIOUS VOICE (O.S.)
          Welcome. We've been expecting you.

Lights suddenly illuminate the space, revealing armed figures.

                    MAIN CHARACTER
                    (to Supporting Character)
          Run!

Chaos erupts as they try to escape.

                    SUPPORTING CHARACTER
                    (while running)
          This way! I see an exit!

SOUND EFFECT: GUNFIRE

They dive for cover behind shipping containers.

                    MAIN CHARACTER
                    (breathing heavily)
          We're pinned down. Any ideas?

                    SUPPORTING CHARACTER
          There's a skylight above us. If we
          can reach it...

                    MAIN CHARACTER
          It's worth a shot.

They prepare for their escape attempt.

                         FADE TO BLACK.

                         SLOW FADE IN:

# ACT III - The Resolution

## Chapter 4: Final Confrontation

= The climactic battle begins

EXT. WAREHOUSE ROOFTOP - MORNING

Our heroes have made it to the roof.

                    MAIN CHARACTER
          We can't keep running forever.
          It's time to end this.

                    SUPPORTING CHARACTER
          Are you sure about this?

                    MAIN CHARACTER
          No. But it's the only way.

They prepare for the final confrontation.

                    MYSTERIOUS FIGURE (O.S.)
          You can't escape! Give up now!

                    MAIN CHARACTER
                    (calling back)
          Never! We'll fight to the end!

The final battle begins.

MONTAGE - THE FINAL BATTLE

A) Heroes fight desperately
B) Villains seem to gain the upper hand
C) Heroes find inner strength
D) Tide turns in favor of the heroes

END MONTAGE

                    MAIN CHARACTER
                    (victorious but exhausted)
          It's over. We did it.

                    SUPPORTING CHARACTER
          Is it really over?

                    MAIN CHARACTER
          For now. But there will always be
          another battle to fight.

They look out over the city as the sun sets.

                    MAIN CHARACTER (CONT'D)
          Come on. Let's go home.

                         IRIS OUT.

                                               FADE OUT.

THE END

